error: Q35 violation: Capsule 'NoAtomicFieldsCapsule' has no atomic fields for poison tracking.

       Self-destruct requires at least one atomic field to track poison state.

       Solutions:
       1. Add `poison_state: AtomicU64` field (recommended)
       2. Add `state: DualAtomicU64` field for full coordination
       3. Use `#[capsule(skip_self_destruct = true)]` with ASSUM justification

       Example fix (Option 1):
       #[repr(C, align(64))]  // Adjust size as needed
       struct NoAtomicFieldsCapsule {
       poison_state: AtomicU64,  // Added for Q35
       // ... existing fields ...
       _padding: [u8; N],  // Adjust padding
       }

       Example fix (Option 3 - stateless capsule opt-out):
       #[capsule(alignment = 64, skip_self_destruct = true)]
       // #ASSUME_STATELESS: Pure SIMD/stateless capsule with no coordination state
       // #VERIFY_STATELESS: Self-destruct not applicable - no shared state to poison
